# Values in public files that look personal but are synthetic or required.
# Tab-separated: rule, path glob (fnmatch; * also crosses /), exact text or * (third-party
# files only), reason. Rules taken from the machine (account, host, machine-id, git-identity)
# can never be listed here, since an entry would publish the value.
home-path	tests/*	/home/tester	the synthetic target user of the sandbox, CI and container tests
home-path	lib/shaffy/sandbox.py	/home/tester	the render sandbox's synthetic home
home-path	.github/workflows/*.yml	/home/tester	CI's unprivileged user, in this repository's and the supplements' workflows
home-path	tests/test_records.py	/home/someone	a record for another target user
home-path	tests/test_system.py	/home/second	a second target user
home-path	tests/test_system.py	/home/u	a minimal record
home-path	tests/test_bootstrap.py	/home/x	a capture path shaped like an Ansible value
home-path	tests/test_home_backup.py	/home/old	a snapshot path from another home
private-ip	tests/vm/vm-post-install.sh	10.0.2.2	QEMU user networking's fixed address for the host, which the VM kit lets reach sshd
email	scripts/install-better-bibtex.py	better-bibtex@iris-advies.com.xpi	Better BibTeX's add-on id, which names its file in Zotero's profile
email	lib/shaffy/updates.py	better-bibtex@iris-advies.com.xpi	Better BibTeX's add-on id, which names its file in Zotero's profile
